# Per-machine Claude Code settings. Holds PIXELLAB_SECRET, which .mcp.json expands into the
# PixelLab MCP server's Authorization header — the committed .mcp.json carries the variable name
# only, never the token.
.claude/settings.local.json

# NOTE (Phase 132): the block that used to sit here described parking eight unused purchased tileset
# packs — "sitting in apps/web/src/assets/tilesets/ at 108 MB and were parked here by the Phase 90
# workflow audit". **That cleanup was never applied.** `git show 49b4130 -- .gitignore` shows the
# commit added this comment and no ignore patterns at all, so nothing was ever parked: all 197 files
# under apps/web/src/assets/tilesets/ are tracked, at 132 MB, and `git ls-files --others` there
# returns nothing. The comment is kept in corrected form rather than deleted, because a reader who
# greps for "parked" needs to find out that it did not happen.
#
# Whether to untrack them is a real, unmade decision and not a documentation fix, so it is left open
# here. Two consumers make a pack load-bearing even though nothing globs it, and both were nearly
# missed the first time: a `from:` source for a derived sheet (or `npm run assets:pack-objects` can
# no longer rebuild what the maps draw), and planned-maps.js's forward slate, which
# tests/unit/tile-palettes.test.js asserts actually exists on disk. `npm run assets:audit` is the
# authoritative check — run it before acting, rather than trusting the numbers in any comment.

# Painted Chronotravel plate sources: ~2.5 MB 1672x941 PNGs, one per destination. The committed
# artefact is apps/web/src/assets/plates/*.webp, built from these by `npm run assets:build-plates`.
# They stay out of git for their size, and out of apps/web/src/assets/ so nothing can reference the
# 2.5 MB copy by accident.
art-source/

# Playwright visual baselines are captured on Windows and committed as *-chromium-win32.png.
# A run on macOS auto-creates a parallel *-chromium-darwin.png set; those are unreviewed
# by definition, and CLAUDE.md's ladder requires reviewing a baseline before accepting it.
tests/e2e/*-snapshots/*-chromium-darwin.png
